  <content class="introduction">
      <figure class="splash" id="Figure01_00_WorldMap">
        <media alt="This image shows a map of the world on a dark background with the continents cutout to reveal a lighter color.
        ">
          <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Figure01_00_WorldMap.jpg"/>
        </media>
      <caption>
        Business ethics do not exist in a vacuum. They are a reflection of the underlying values of a society and the way society lives out those values over time. This experience is captured in language, culture, religious traditions, and modes of thinking, all of which have varied throughout history and influence the conduct of business in a range of ways. (credit: modification of “atlas close up dark dirty” by Aaditya Arora/Pexels, CC0)
        </caption>
      </figure>
    <section id="sect-00001">

      <para id="para-00002">
        “This king is the greatest of the Muslim kings of the Sudan.”<footnote id="foot-00001">Here used as a geographical term meaning “land of the blacks.” WW-test notes this is a footnote and should appear at the bottom of the page.</footnote> The line between early and middle adulthood is difficult to define. The physical and cognitive changes experienced during this transition tend to be gradual occurring over years. To add to the confusion of middle adulthood, many adults of both middle and older age groups report feeling younger than their chronological age (Chopik et al., 2018). For the most part this chapter will discuss middle age as a time between 30 and 59.
      </para>
      <para id="para-00003">
        One question among many posed in a study on closeness is “If you were going to live to the age of 90, and retain either the mind or the body of a 30-year-old for the last 60 years of your life, which would you want?” (Aron et al., 1997). Asking this to others, some people respond readily, while others take a moment to think. Some abilities you have learned about peaked in early adulthood, but some skills may continue to develop in middle adulthood while others begin to decline. As you go through this chapter, hopefully, your view point on this question will be shaped. WW-test notes this opener is 222 words.
      </para>

    </section>
  </content>
